course: dictionary
lesson: 3577
title: Feverish: two meanings, one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Mia felt feverish, so she stayed in bed with a glass of water.» A feverish person has a fever: their body is hotter than normal, and they often feel shivery and unwell. Normal body temperature is about 37 °C, so a feverish body is warmer than that.
explain: Feverish has a second meaning too: very fast, excited and nervous. «The team worked feverishly before the deadline.» Nobody has a fever there. The team is working very fast because time is nearly up. Ask which meaning fits the rest of the sentence, then try it.
explain: Feverishly is the adverb, the word that tells you how something is done. «He searched feverishly for his lost ticket» means he searched in a fast, anxious way. The clues are in the words around it, and the word lost tells you why he was in a hurry.
fact: Feverish is an adjective: a feverish child, feverish dreams, feverish excitement.
fact: «Feverish» means having a fever: a body temperature higher than normal, with feeling hot, shivery and unwell.
fact: «Feverish» also means very fast, excited or nervous, as in «feverish activity».
fact: «Feverishly» is the adverb: «She searched feverishly for her keys.»
fact: If you feel feverish, rest, drink water and tell an adult. Normal body temperature is about 37 °C.
exercise: «Mia felt feverish and shivery, so she stayed in bed.» What does feverish mean here? | *Having a fever, feeling hot and unwell | Very excited about a trip | Full of energy after a long sleep | Running fast in the park
exercise: «The engineers worked feverishly to finish the bridge before the storm.» What does feverishly suggest? | In a cold, shivery way | Slowly and calmly, with plenty of time | Sleepily, after a long rest | *Very fast and nervously, as if time was running out
exercise: «Bundling a feverish child in blankets can make them overheat; light clothes and a cool room are better.» What is the better idea for a feverish child? | Pile on thick blankets to sweat it out | Hot rooms with the windows shut | Cold baths straight away | *Light clothes and a cool room
test: «The crowd was feverish with excitement as the winner was announced.» What does feverish mean here? | Quiet and calm | Having a fever and shivering | Sleepy and slow | *Full of fast, nervous excitement
test: In «He searched feverishly for his lost ticket», which word is the adverb? | searched | lost | ticket | *feverishly
exam: Mrs Patel says, «If you feel feverish, stay home.» What should a feverish child do? | Take a cold bath and go back to play | *Rest, drink water and tell an adult | Play outside until they sweat it off | Go to school and hide the feeling
